.IX Title "Lucy::Search::Searcher 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Search::Searcher 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Search::Searcher \- Base class for searching collections of documents.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    # Abstract base class.
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Abstract base class for objects which search.  Core subclasses include
IndexSearcher and
PolySearcher.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 7
\&    package MySearcher;
\&    use base qw( Lucy::Search::Searcher );
\&    sub new {
\&        my $self = shift\->SUPER::new;
\&        ...
\&        return $self;
\&    }
.Ve
.PP
Abstract constructor.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBschema\fR \- A Schema.
.SH "ABSTRACT METHODS"
.IX Header "ABSTRACT METHODS"
.SS doc_max
.IX Subsection "doc_max"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $searcher\->doc_max();
.Ve
.PP
Return the maximum number of docs in the collection represented by the
Searcher, which is also the highest possible internal doc id.
Documents which have been marked as deleted but not yet purged are
included in this count.
.SS doc_freq
.IX Subsection "doc_freq"
.Vb 4
\&    my $int = $searcher\->doc_freq(
\&        field => $field,  # required
\&        term  => $term,   # required
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Return the number of documents which contain the term in the given
field.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBfield\fR \- Field name.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBterm\fR \- The term to look up.
.SS collect
.IX Subsection "collect"
.Vb 4
\&    $searcher\->collect(
\&        query     => $query,      # required
\&        collector => $collector,  # required
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Iterate over hits, feeding them into a
Collector.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBquery\fR \- A Query.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBcollector\fR \- A Collector.
.SS fetch_doc
.IX Subsection "fetch_doc"
.Vb 1
\&    my $hit_doc = $searcher\->fetch_doc($doc_id);
.Ve
.PP
Retrieve a document.  Throws an error if the doc id is out of range.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBdoc_id\fR \- A document id.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS glean_query
.IX Subsection "glean_query"
.Vb 2
\&    my $query = $searcher\->glean_query($query);
\&    my $query = $searcher\->glean_query();  # default: undef
.Ve
.PP
If the supplied object is a Query, return it; if it’s a query string,
create a QueryParser and parse it to produce a query against all
indexed fields.
.SS hits
.IX Subsection "hits"
.Vb 6
\&    my $hits = $searcher\->hits(
\&        query      => $query,       # required
\&        offset     => $offset,      # default: 0
\&        num_wanted => $num_wanted,  # default: 10
\&        sort_spec  => $sort_spec,   # default: undef
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Return a Hits object containing the top results.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBquery\fR \- Either a Query object or a query string.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBoffset\fR \- The number of most-relevant hits to discard, typically
used when “paging” through hits N at a time.  Setting
\&\f(CW\*(C`offset\*(C'\fR to 20 and \f(CW\*(C`num_wanted\*(C'\fR to 10 retrieves
hits 21\-30, assuming that 30 hits can be found.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBnum_wanted\fR \- The number of hits you would like to see after
\&\f(CW\*(C`offset\*(C'\fR is taken into account.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBsort_spec\fR \- A SortSpec, which will affect
how results are ranked and returned.
.SS get_schema
.IX Subsection "get_schema"
.Vb 1
\&    my $schema = $searcher\->get_schema();
.Ve
.PP
Accessor for the object’s \f(CW\*(C`schema\*(C'\fR member.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Search::Searcher isa Clownfish::Obj.
